.\" Short English fallback page; the full manual is in French (dada.fr.8).
.TH DADA 8 "November 2026" "tolome-dada" "System administration"
.SH NAME
dada \- run a command with administrator rights
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dada
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR]...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dada
("His Majesty" in Fon) is the administration command of Tolome. It runs a command
as another user, \fIroot\fR by default, through
.BR sudo\-rs (8),
with exactly the same arguments. The authorization policy stays in
.I /etc/sudoers
and
.IR /etc/sudoers.d .
The classic
.BR sudo (8)
command stays installed and unchanged. Removing the package \fBtolome\-dada\fR
only removes \fBdada\fR.
.PP
All options are those of
.BR sudo\-rs (8).
The complete manual is available in French:
.B man \-L fr dada
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dada nala install vim
dada apt update
dada \-i
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sudo\-rs (8),
.BR sudoers (5),
.BR nala (8),
.BR apt (8)
